From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:10:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] check this setup: settings a card could not put back are said
 as its own

The A/B comparison of native Dolby Vision and the frame packing card
change settings of Kodi for a while (the form of Dolby Vision, the 3D
settings) and put them back afterwards, the journal first, so that the
next start puts back what could not be set now. Where one could not be
set, both said string 33741 of the passthrough check: "Some sound
settings could not be set now: when Kodi starts again, they are set as
this check decided". Neither is a sound setting, and they are put back
as they were before the card, not as it decided. They now say 33840:
some settings that this check changed for a while could not be put back
now, and the next start sets them as they were before it (English, and
the three Spanish ones). The passthrough check keeps 33741, which is
right for it.

"Your display" writes its journal twice: what the settings were before
the change, then, once every setting is set, the journal of what the
choices now change. The second write was the only one not guarded: where
the storage could not be written at that moment, the exception ended the
step after the settings were set, without keeping the choices or saying
what was set. It is logged now, and the journal written before the
change stays, which still holds every value from before it.

Host tests (stand-ins for Kodi, tools/regress kodi-host): a setting
that cannot be put back after the comparison and after the card, and a
second journal write that fails. They fail without this change and pass
with it.
---
